1
00:00:01,794 --> 00:00:03,253
Hi.

2
00:00:03,295 --> 00:00:04,421
Hey!
Oh, my God!

3
00:00:04,463 --> 00:00:06,214
Welcome back.
How was the honeymoon?

4
00:00:06,256 --> 00:00:07,925
Oh, incredible.

5
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,636
Oh, champagne,
candlelit dinners,

6
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:12,387
moonlight walks on the beach.

7
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:14,473
It was so romantic.

8
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:15,683
So where's Mike?

9
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:17,100
Oh, he's at the doctor.

10
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,477
He didn't poop
the whole time we were there.

11
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,481
Well, anyway,
I'm glad you're back.

12
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:24,191
I really need your help.
Oh, why? What's up?

13
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:25,693
Well, I have an audition
for this play,

14
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,486
and for some of it,
I have to speak French.

15
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:31,657
Which, according to my resume,
I'm fluent in.

16
00:00:31,699 --> 00:00:33,701
Joey, you shouldn't lie
on your resume.

17
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:36,077
Yeah, you really shouldn't.

18
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:38,539
By the way, how was that
yearlong dig in Cairo?

19
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:41,959
( softly ):
It was okay.

20
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:45,004
I did not know
you spoke French.

21
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:47,673
Oui, bien sur
je parle francais.

22
00:00:47,715 --> 00:00:48,966
( continues speaking French )

23
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:51,301
Oh. You're so sexy.

24
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,803
JOEY:
So will you help me?

25
00:00:52,845 --> 00:00:54,805
I really want to be
in this play.
Sure.

26
00:00:54,847 --> 00:00:57,265
( speaking French )

27
00:00:57,307 --> 00:01:00,185
Seriously, stop it
or I'm gonna jump on you.

28
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:11,572
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

29
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:14,282
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

30
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,451
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

31
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:21,582
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

32
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,918
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

33
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:26,378
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

34
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:30,089
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

35
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:35,930
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

36
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:43,353
Hey.
Hey.

37
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:46,273
Why are you wearing
my apron?

38
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:47,900
I'm making cookies for Erica.

39
00:01:47,942 --> 00:01:49,735
By the way, we have to leave
for the airport soon.

40
00:01:49,777 --> 00:01:51,445
Her plane comes in
in about an hour.

41
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:54,698
Oh, hey, when she gets here, is
it okay if I introduce you two

42
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,618
as my wife, and the woman
who's carrying my child?

43
00:01:58,911 --> 00:02:00,454
No?

44
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:02,205
Divorce?

45
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:05,709
Hey.
Hey.

46
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:07,086
You guys know where Rachel is?

47
00:02:07,127 --> 00:02:08,629
I haven't seen her
since this morning.

48
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,171
It's unbelievable.

49
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:11,840
She was supposed to meet me
a half hour ago with Emma.

50
00:02:11,882 --> 00:02:12,841
Hey.

51
00:02:12,883 --> 00:02:14,051
Hey!

52
00:02:14,093 --> 00:02:15,343
These are for Erica.

53
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:17,554
What, she's going to eat
all those cookies?

54
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:21,683
Well, I want the baby to
come out all cute and fat.

55
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:25,104
So why is Erica coming to visit?

56
00:02:25,144 --> 00:02:26,730
Because we want to get
to know her better, and, uh...

57
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:28,148
Plus, she's never been
to New York,

58
00:02:28,189 --> 00:02:29,858
so she's wants to see
all the tourist spots:

59
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,860
the Statue of Liberty
and Empire State Building...

60
00:02:31,902 --> 00:02:34,029
Those places,
there's always so many people,

61
00:02:34,071 --> 00:02:36,197
and they're being corralled
like cattle.

62
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:40,410
And there's always
some idiot who goes "moo."

63
00:02:40,452 --> 00:02:43,747
Well, if it annoys you so much,
then why do you do it?

64
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,208
Oh, hi. Hi.

65
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,503
Thanks for showing up
30 minutes late.

66
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,880
Ross...
No, no, no, I'm sure
you have a great excuse.

67
00:02:51,922 --> 00:02:53,674
What was it,
a hair appointment?

68
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,050
A mani-pedi?

69
00:02:55,092 --> 00:02:56,927
Was there a sale at Barney's?

70
00:02:56,969 --> 00:03:00,263
My father had a heart attack...

71
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,641
while I was at Barney's.

72
00:03:05,393 --> 00:03:07,104
Oh, my God.
Honey...

73
00:03:07,146 --> 00:03:08,271
I'm so sorry.

74
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,523
Is he okay?

75
00:03:09,564 --> 00:03:11,025
Yeah, they said
he's going to be fine,

76
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:12,651
but he's still
heavily sedated.

77
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:13,777
Okay, okay, I'm going
to come out

78
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:15,112
to Long Island with you.

79
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:16,488
I mean, you can't be alone
right now.

80
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:19,282
No, come on,
I'm totally okay.

81
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,869
( cries ):
I don't need you to come.

82
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,871
I can totally
handle this on my own.

83
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:27,958
Still, still, let me
come... for me.

84
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,961
Okay, if you
really need to.

85
00:03:31,003 --> 00:03:32,337
I bet someone could use

86
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:34,464
one of Monica's
freshly baked cookies.

87
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:36,925
( gasps ):
Oh, I really could.

88
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,185
All right, this seems
pretty simple.

89
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:48,353
Your first line is,
"My name is Claude."

90
00:03:48,395 --> 00:03:50,647
So just repeat after me.

91
00:03:50,689 --> 00:03:52,273
Je m'appelle Claude.

92
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:56,111
Je de coup, plau.

93
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:00,239
Well, let's just...
let's try it again.

94
00:04:00,281 --> 00:04:01,324
Okay.

95
00:04:01,366 --> 00:04:03,202
Je m'appelle Claude.

96
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:05,871
Je de ple, mloo.

97
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:08,707
Huh.

98
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:12,127
It's not quite
what I'm saying.

99
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:13,837
Really?

100
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:16,173
Sounds exactly
the same to me.

101
00:04:16,215 --> 00:04:17,298
It does, really?

102
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,842
Yeah.

103
00:04:18,884 --> 00:04:20,427
All right, let's just
try it again.

104
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:23,055
Really listen.
Got it.

105
00:04:23,097 --> 00:04:25,599
( slowly ):
Okay. Je m'appelle Claude.

106
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:29,019
Je da flup, flee.

107
00:04:29,061 --> 00:04:31,188
Oh, mon dieu.

108
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:32,439
Oh, de foof.

109
00:04:34,108 --> 00:04:35,859
Hey, you guys.

110
00:04:35,901 --> 00:04:37,318
Hi.
Hi.
Hey.

111
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,696
I want you to meet
someone really special.

112
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:41,782
Phoebe, this is Erica.

113
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,617
And this is the baby.

114
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:45,535
Joey... Erica. Baby.

115
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:46,661
Hi.
Hi.

116
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:49,206
Everyone...
Erica. Baby.

117
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:51,959
Monica. Calm. Self.

118
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,293
JOEY:
Hey, sit down.

119
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:54,586
There you go.
Thank you.

120
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:56,004
It's really nice
to meet you guys.

121
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:57,505
I can't believe
I'm here.

122
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:58,757
Welcome to New York City.

123
00:04:58,799 --> 00:04:59,758
Or should I say...

124
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:02,719
Gue de floof,
New York City.

125
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:05,806
Why would you
say that?

126
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,268
Okay, what are you going
to be doing today?

127
00:05:09,308 --> 00:05:11,186
Well, I want to see everything:

128
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:14,397
Times Square, Coney Island,
Rockefeller Center.

129
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:15,774
Oh, you know what you should do?

130
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:16,733
You should walk all
the way to the top

131
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:17,692
of the Statue of Liberty.

132
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,318
Oh, yeah, let's do that.

133
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,737
Great.

134
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:22,781
This baby better be really good.

135
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:30,747
Hi. Excuse me, I'm here
to see my father.

136
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:32,082
My name is Rachel Green.

137
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,959
And I'm Dr. Ross Geller.
Ross,

138
00:05:34,001 --> 00:05:35,585
please, this is
a hospital, okay.

139
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:37,587
That actually means
something here.

140
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:39,881
So can we please go in?

141
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:41,382
Absolutely.

142
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,260
Rach, I think I'm gonna
wait out here because, uh...

143
00:05:43,302 --> 00:05:45,095
my throat is feeling
a little scratchy.

144
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:46,513
I don't want to infect him.

145
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:48,598
Ross, please, don't be
so scared of him.

146
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,226
I'm not scared of him,
I'm really sick.

147
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,270
He's under sedation,
so he's pretty much out.

148
00:05:53,312 --> 00:05:54,562
I'm feeling better.

149
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,357
( gasps )

150
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:00,152
Oh, my God.

151
00:06:00,194 --> 00:06:02,445
Oh. Oh, wow,

152
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:04,447
that ear and nose
hair trimmer I got him

153
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:07,408
was just money
down the drain, huh?

154
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,078
Ms. Green, your father's doctor
is on the phone

155
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,830
if you'd like to speak to him.

156
00:06:11,872 --> 00:06:13,665
Oh, great.
Are you going to be okay?

157
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,583
He's unconscious.
I think we'll be just fine.

158
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,793
Okay.

159
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:33,352
( horses neigh, dinosaur roars)

160
00:06:39,191 --> 00:06:40,984
( roars )

161
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:45,947
( chuckles )

162
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:55,999
Um, did... did the TV wake you?

163
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:57,334
No.

164
00:06:57,376 --> 00:06:59,378
When you put your feet up
on my bed,

165
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:01,838
you tugged on my catheter.

166
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:08,053
Ouchie.

167
00:07:08,095 --> 00:07:10,680
What are you doing here, Geller?

168
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:13,641
I came with Rachel,
who should be back any second.

169
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,727
So what's new?

170
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:18,521
Oh, I had a little heart attack.

171
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,690
Right. Is it painful?

172
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:24,027
What, the heart attack,
or sitting here talking to you?

173
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:25,695
( chuckles nervously )

174
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:28,240
Let's see if we can get
that Rachel back here.

175
00:07:28,282 --> 00:07:29,657
So what's new
with you?

176
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:32,369
Knocked up any more
of my daughters lately?

177
00:07:32,411 --> 00:07:34,413
Nope. Just the one.
Rach!

178
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:39,000
Je m'appelle Claude.

179
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:41,044
Je dup kol, mlu.

180
00:07:41,086 --> 00:07:42,170
No!

181
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:43,964
Okay.

182
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,049
Maybe if we just break it down.

183
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:48,885
Okay, let's just... let's try it
one syllable at a time.

184
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:51,054
Okay, so repeat after me.

185
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,097
Je.

186
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,098
Je.

187
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,099
M'a.
M'a.

188
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:55,809
Pelle.
Pelle.

189
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:56,726
Great.
Okay, faster.

190
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:57,727
Je.
Je.

191
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:58,645
M'a.
M'a.

192
00:07:58,686 --> 00:07:59,771
Pelle.
Pelle.

193
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:01,564
Je m'appelle.
Me poo poo.

194
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:05,693
Okay, it's too hard.

195
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:06,736
I can't teach you.

196
00:08:06,778 --> 00:08:08,322
What are you doing?

197
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:10,782
I have to go before
I put your head through a wall.

198
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:12,451
No, no! Don't go.
I need you.

199
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:14,577
My audition is tomorrow.

200
00:08:14,619 --> 00:08:16,746
Ja blu bla!

201
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,873
Me la pee!

202
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:21,835
Oom blah!

203
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,837
Poo.

204
00:08:31,136 --> 00:08:32,887
Hey.
Hi.

205
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,597
I was going to make us
some dinner,

206
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,350
but all I found in
your dad's fridge

207
00:08:36,391 --> 00:08:37,976
was bacon and heavy cream.

208
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:40,645
I think we solved the mystery
of the heart attack.

209
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,856
Did you call your parents?

210
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,024
Oh, yeah.
Emma's doing great.

211
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,318
Oh, good.

212
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,986
Wow.

213
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:49,363
What?

214
00:08:49,404 --> 00:08:52,824
Just can't believe
I'm in Rachel Green's room.

215
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:55,618
What do you mean?
You've been in my room before.

216
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:59,080
Yeah, sure, right.

217
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:01,666
Like I'd ever be
in Rachel Green's room.

218
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,460
Okay, I gotta tell you,
it's really weird

219
00:09:03,502 --> 00:09:04,794
when you use my whole name.

220
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:06,629
Sorry.

221
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,632
You okay?

222
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:10,675
Yeah.

223
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:11,885
You had a rough day, huh?

224
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:13,387
Yeah.

225
00:09:13,428 --> 00:09:15,722
Just so weird seeing him
like that, you know?

226
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:17,057
I mean, he's a doctor.

227
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:20,185
You don't expect
doctors to get sick.

228
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:22,354
But we do.

229
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,360
You know,
he's going to be okay, Rach.

230
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:34,032
Oh, I don't want him
to wake up alone.

231
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,867
I should go to the hospital.

232
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,869
No, no.
Hey, hey, hey, look.

233
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:39,871
What?
They gave him a
lot of medication, okay?

234
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:41,831
He wouldn't even know
if you were there.

235
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:44,834
We'll go see him first
thing in the morning, okay?

236
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:46,836
Really?
I shouldn't feel guilty?

237
00:09:46,878 --> 00:09:48,922
No. Hey, Rach, you've been
an amazing daughter, okay?

238
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:51,341
Right now you just need
to get some rest.

239
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:53,510
Okay, maybe you're right.

240
00:09:53,552 --> 00:09:55,429
Good night.

241
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:59,140
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

242
00:09:59,182 --> 00:10:02,769
Would you stay here with me
for a little while?

243
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,729
Sure.

244
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:05,813
Okay.

245
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:09,568
Thank you for coming
with me today.

246
00:10:09,608 --> 00:10:11,111
Oh, of course.

247
00:10:11,152 --> 00:10:14,322
Rachel Green is very
happy you're in her room.

248
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:16,741
Me, too.

249
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:17,992
Come here.

250
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:22,747
I just don't want
to be alone tonight.

251
00:10:22,789 --> 00:10:24,207
Okay, well, um...

252
00:10:24,249 --> 00:10:27,794
I can maybe grab
a sleeping bag or...

253
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:40,265
Oh...

254
00:10:40,307 --> 00:10:41,975
Oh.

255
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:45,812
No, Rach!

256
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,188
I'm sorry, I just...

257
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:49,524
I just don't think this...
this is a good idea.

258
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:52,735
Well, we won't know that
until we do it, will we?

259
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:57,449
Uh, look, um, you are upset
about your father

260
00:10:57,491 --> 00:10:59,493
and you're feeling vulnerable.

261
00:10:59,534 --> 00:11:01,702
And I just don't feel
